me":"B. Point"},"type":"shooter"},{"athlete":{"id":"4697705","displayName":"Dylan Garand","shortName":"D. Garand"}}]}],"gameInfo":{"venue":{"id":"1830","fullName":"Madison Square Garden","address":{"city":"New York","state":"NY","country":"USA"},"grass":false,"images":[{"href":"https://a.espncdn.com/i/venues/nhl/day/1830.jpg","width":2000,"height":1125,"alt":"","rel":["full","day"]}]},"attendance":17076,"officials":[{"fullName":"Francois St. Laurent","displayName":"Francois St. Laurent","position":{"name":"Referee","displayName":"Referee","id":"24"},"order":0},{"fullName":"Chris Schlenker","displayName":"Chris Schlenker","position":{"name":"Referee","displayName":"Referee","id":"24"},"order":0},{"fullName":"CJ Murray","displayName":"CJ Murray","position":{"name":"Linesman","displayName":"Linesman","id":"25"},"order":0},{"fullName":"Brandon Grillo","displayName":"Brandon Grillo","position":{"name":"Linesman","displayName":"Linesman","id":"25"},"order":0}]},"article":{"headline":"Alexis Lafreniere scores twice as Rangers beat Lightning 4-1","description":"— Alexis Lafreniere scored twice and Dylan Garand made 25 saves as the New York Rangers beat the Tampa Bay Lightning 4-1 on Tuesday night for their fifth straight home win.","story":"NEW YORK -- — <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4697382/alexis-lafreniere\">Alexis Lafreniere</a> scored twice and <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4697705/dylan-garand\">Dylan Garand</a> made 25 saves as the <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/team/_/name/nyr/new-york-rangers\">New York Rangers</a> beat the <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/team/_/name/tb/tampa-bay-lightning\">Tampa Bay Lightning</a> 4-1 on Tuesday night for their fifth straight home win.\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4697468/will-cuylle\">Will Cuylle</a> and <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/2562637/mika-zibanejad\">Mika Zibanejad</a> also scored for the Rangers, who snapped Tampa Bay’s four-game winning streak. The Lightning hadn’t lost since falling to the Rangers 5-1 in New York’s home opener on Oct. 1.\n\n\r\n              Lafreniere scored 62 seconds into the game, beating Lightning goaltender <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/2976847/andrei-vasilevskiy\">Andrei Vasilevskiy</a> from in close.\n\n\r\n              The 25-year-old Lafreniere, the first pick in the 2020 NHL draft, scored again at 12:47 of the first, his team-leading seventh goal.\n\n\r\n              Ty Kartye assisted on both of Lafreniere's goals. Kartye also scored twice in New York’s previous game, a 6-2 home win over Vancouver.\n\n\r\n              Tampa Bay’s <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/2968829/zemgus-girgensons\">Zemgus Girgensons</a> narrowed the deficit to 2-1 with his first goal of the season late in the first.\n\n\r\n              Cuylle made it 3-1 late in the second, redirecting a shot by <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4378683/sean-durzi\">Sean Durzi</a> from the point past Vasilevskiy for his third goal.\n\n\r\n              Zibanejad had an empty-netter at 17:16 of the third.\n\n\r\n              Lafreniere, who had a hat trick in a 5-2 home win over the Islanders on Oct. 6, has goals in four straight games. His career high in goals was 28 in 2023-24.\n\n\r\n              It's just the third time the Rangers have won five straight home games to start a season. They won six straight in 1983-84 and eight in a row to begin the 1990-91 campaign.\n\n\r\n              Garand won his second straight since starting goaltender <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/3151297/igor-shesterkin\">Igor Shesterkin</a> was injured last Friday at Washington and declared out for the season the next day.\n\n\r\n              The 24-year-old was serenaded with chants of “Dylan, Dylan,” after he made several key saves in the third period.\n\n\r\n              Vasilevskiy made 19 saves.\n\n\r\n              <hl2>Up next</hl2>\r\n              Rangers: At New Jersey on Thursday.\n\n\r\n              Lightning: Host Seattle on Thursday.\n\n\r\n              ------\n\n\r\n              \r\n                <a href=\"https://apnews.com/hub/nhl\">See AP’s full NHL coverage here</a>","published":"2026-10-14T02:07:27Z"}}